# Melbing C# architecture

Follow [GUIDELINES.md](../../GUIDELINES.md). Summary:

## Layers

- **Domain** — entities only
- **Application** — use cases, DTOs, interfaces, validation (no EF/SQLite/JSON converters)
- **Infrastructure** — DB, repositories, serialization adapters (ESP32 bools, etc.)
- **Web** — HTTP, Razor, host registration

Dependencies: `Web → Infrastructure → Application → Domain`. Never reverse. Application must not reference Infrastructure.

## Placement

- Technical adapters (persistence, external JSON formats) go in **Infrastructure**, even if they contain “logic”.
- Register adapters from Web (`AddEsp32Converters()`, DI), do not hang Infrastructure types on Application DTOs.
- Gray zones: choose deliberately; prefer a thinner Application and push technical detail out.

## ESP32 contract

Keep `POST /api/log` snake_case + numeric bool compatibility; adapt on the server, do not break firmware.
